---
const rows = [
  {
    claim: 'An AI disproved an 80-year-old Erdős conjecture',
    verdict: 'confirmed',
    reality:
      'The conjectured near-linear upper bound n^(1+o(1)) is false. Nine mathematicians read the argument and did not find a gap.'
  },
  {
    claim: 'The unit distance problem is now solved',
    verdict: 'false',
    reality:
      'The gap between the n^(1+delta) construction and the O(n^4/3) upper bound is wider than ever. The problem is more open, not less.'
  },
  {
    claim: 'The model worked autonomously',
    verdict: 'partly',
    reality:
      'The problem was chosen by humans from a curated list and the prompt suggested looking for a counterexample. Reports describe the argument itself as produced in a single run.'
  },
  {
    claim: 'The proof was formally verified',
    verdict: 'partly',
    reality:
      'A Lean 4 formalisation was completed a month later by a separate group, conditional on two classical theorems not yet in Mathlib.'
  },
  {
    claim: 'The exponent is n^1.014',
    verdict: 'not the model',
    reality:
      'The model gave an inexplicit delta > 0. The 1.014 figure is Will Sawin, in an independent preprint. Later certificate searches push it further.'
  },
  {
    claim: 'It was peer reviewed',
    verdict: 'pending',
    reality:
      'Expert scrutiny was immediate and public, but journal review had not concluded. Gowers said he would have recommended acceptance without hesitation.'
  }
]
---

<figure class="viz claims-viz" aria-labelledby="unit-distance-claims-title">
  <figcaption id="unit-distance-claims-title">
    <strong>What was claimed against what was confirmed</strong>
    <span>Six statements that circulated in May 2026, graded against the primary sources.</span>
  </figcaption>

  <div class="table" role="table" aria-label="Claims and their status">
    <div class="row head" role="row">
      <span role="columnheader">Claim as circulated</span>
      <span role="columnheader">Status</span>
      <span role="columnheader">What the sources support</span>
    </div>
    {
      rows.map((r) => (
        <div class="row" role="row">
          <strong role="cell">{r.claim}</strong>
          <span class="verdict" data-verdict={r.verdict} role="cell">
            {r.verdict}
          </span>
          <p role="cell">{r.reality}</p>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</figure>

<style>
  .viz {
    container-type: inline-size;
    margin: 2em 0;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--astro-code-background);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  figcaption {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.15rem;
  }
  figcaption strong {
    font: 600 var(--font-size-s) var(--mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  figcaption span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font: 0.7rem/1.5 var(--mono);
  }
  .table {
    display: grid;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--text-secondary);
  }
  .row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) 7rem minmax(0, 1.5fr);
    gap: 0.5rem 1rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: 0.75rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .row.head span {
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    font: 0.6rem var(--mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .row strong {
    font: 600 0.78rem/1.4 var(--sans);
  }
  .row p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font: 0.66rem/1.6 var(--mono);
  }
  .verdict {
    justify-self: start;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.45rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font: 0.6rem var(--mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .verdict[data-verdict='confirmed'] {
    border-color: var(--text-primary);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .verdict[data-verdict='false'] {
    border-style: dashed;
    border-color: var(--text-primary);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  @container (max-width: 600px) {
    .row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.4rem;
    }
    .row.head {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
